# a_forecast_holding_later_crosses_whole
#
# EVERY PUBLIC GRAPH WHATEVER ITS PERIOD (#619). A pass asks its rules at instants of its own —
# a step's landing, a want's instant — so a forecast holding hours from now is a graph the
# PRESENT has not reached and the search still must be able to see.
#
# Copied whole, the imagined world's own door filters by the instant it is asked at, exactly as
# the belief base's does. Copied at now, a search could not see past the present's weather, and
# would find nothing there rather than an error — which is this function's whole failure mode.
#
# So the forecast crosses even though its period starts in three hours, and the diff shows it
# unchanged. A version of this that filtered by the clock would show it DROPPED.
#
# The clock stands at 2026-01-01T12:00:00Z.

@prefix : <http://example.org/test#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix deliberation: <http://example.org/orexis/deliberation#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

GRAPH :world {
  :tank1 a :Tank .
}

GRAPH :forecast {
  :outside :warmth 28 .
}

GRAPH :catalogue {
  :catalogue a orexis:CatalogueGraph .
  :catalogue a orexis:Graph .
  :forecast a orexis:Graph .
  :forecast a orexis:PublicGraph .
  :forecast dcterms:temporal _:b1 .
  :ontology a orexis:Graph .
  :ontology a orexis:OntologyGraph .
  :ontology a orexis:PublicGraph .
  :world a orexis:Graph .
  :world a orexis:PublicGraph .
  _:b1 a dcterms:PeriodOfTime .
  _:b1 orexis:end "2026-01-01T18:00:00+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .
  _:b1 orexis:start "2026-01-01T15:00:00+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .
}
